1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:02,700
Sync and Corrected by ZOTAL
www.zotal.info

2
00:00:02,828 --> 00:00:03,903
(crow caws)

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:06,076
<i>(Frankie)</i> <i>Ah, Valentine's Day...
</i> (Snap)

4
00:00:06,212 --> 00:00:08,779
<i>The official end of Christmas.</i>
You know,

5
00:00:08,865 --> 00:00:11,088
we really should start taking
the Christmas tree down sooner.

6
00:00:11,232 --> 00:00:12,744
Look around.
We should do a lotta things.

7
00:00:12,872 --> 00:00:13,777
(Door opens and closes)

8
00:00:14,256 --> 00:00:16,807
This whole school business
is grueling.

9
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:19,157
I just turned in
a book report on "Artemis Fowl."

10
00:00:19,264 --> 00:00:21,666
Now she's making us
write a paper on love.

11
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,833
I'm 10. I don't know
anything about love.

12
00:00:24,913 --> 00:00:26,418
Well, that's what
the Internet's for.

13
00:00:26,509 --> 00:00:28,832
Just get on it, type in "love,"
and see what comes up.

14
00:00:28,923 --> 00:00:30,871
You know what? Never mind.

15
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:34,438
Hey, what are you guys
doing for Valentine's Day?

16
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:36,203
Maybe I could
write my paper about that.

17
00:00:36,302 --> 00:00:38,787
(Chuckles)
That'd be one sad story...

18
00:00:38,896 --> 00:00:41,141
'Cause we're not
doing anything, right?

19
00:00:41,311 --> 00:00:43,168
I didn't plan anything.

20
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:46,149
I-I guess I could
plan something.

21
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:48,171
I will... if you want me to.

22
00:00:48,286 --> 00:00:51,092
I don't know.
I guess, if you want to.

23
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,739
Do you want to go to dinner
or something?

24
00:00:52,832 --> 00:00:55,355
Nah, lot of people,
long wait...

25
00:00:55,503 --> 00:00:56,989
Movie?

26
00:00:57,143 --> 00:00:59,893
We'll fall asleep. We could
do that at home for free.

27
00:00:59,996 --> 00:01:03,233
How about we just stay home?
We know we love each other.

28
00:01:03,385 --> 00:01:05,448
We don't need to shower
and put on control top pantyhose

29
00:01:05,537 --> 00:01:06,426
to prove it.

30
00:01:06,557 --> 00:01:07,972
And since it's Valentine's,

31
00:01:08,099 --> 00:01:09,611
I can bring home
a bucket of chicken...

32
00:01:09,705 --> 00:01:12,675
Unless you want candy
or flowers or something.

33
00:01:12,774 --> 00:01:14,681
Eh, waste of money.
Just the chicken's good.

34
00:01:14,763 --> 00:01:15,723
We'll eat in our sweats

35
00:01:15,789 --> 00:01:17,519
and fall asleep
in front of the TV.

36
00:01:17,624 --> 00:01:18,534
Sounds like a date.

37
00:01:18,615 --> 00:01:20,863
Wait. You're gonna
want to watch sports.

38
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,256
Separate rooms?

39
00:01:22,347 --> 00:01:25,662
Done. Bucket of chicken,
sweats, TV, separate rooms.

40
00:01:25,787 --> 00:01:27,649
Yeah, ooh, we still got it.

41
00:01:28,392 --> 00:01:30,043
(Sighs) Guess I'm hitting
the Internet.

42
00:01:30,172 --> 00:01:33,127
Is your parental control
password still "1-2-3-4"?

43
00:01:33,932 --> 00:01:34,588
(Door opens and closes)

44
00:01:34,684 --> 00:01:36,246
Well, I just got
the lamest assignment ever.

45
00:01:36,328 --> 00:01:37,693
Get in line.

46
00:01:38,493 --> 00:01:42,306
Mrs. Johnson is forcing us
to write a speech or do a video

47
00:01:42,395 --> 00:01:45,571
on a life-changing event,
something I haven't had.

48
00:01:45,809 --> 00:01:46,921
I mean, people who meet me

49
00:01:47,041 --> 00:01:49,350
have the life-changing event
'cause of my awesomeness,

50
00:01:49,432 --> 00:01:51,484
but I can't very well
meet myself, now, can I?

51
00:01:51,802 --> 00:01:52,842
What am I gonna do?

52
00:01:53,055 --> 00:01:54,159
Wait till the last minute,

53
00:01:54,268 --> 00:01:56,505
and turn in something that
squeaks you by with a C minus?

54
00:01:56,678 --> 00:01:58,198
Yeah, that was totally my plan,

55
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,446
but then I found out
this is, like, 30% of my grade.

56
00:02:00,549 --> 00:02:04,895
I mean, that's more than half,
and I got nothing-- Nothing.

57
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:06,522
(Sighs) Axl, you're only 17.

58
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,843
Nobody expects
an Earth-shattering story.

59
00:02:08,942 --> 00:02:10,902
Just think of something
that was meaningful to you

60
00:02:11,009 --> 00:02:12,282
and write about that.

61
00:02:12,395 --> 00:02:13,803
You know what's life-changing?

62
00:02:13,912 --> 00:02:16,669
Helping your dad
snap this tree into 400 pieces

63
00:02:16,756 --> 00:02:18,134
so it'll fit
in the trash barrel.

64
00:02:20,511 --> 00:02:22,096
Would you like to buy
a Valentine's carnation?

65
00:02:22,221 --> 00:02:23,233
The white ones
are for your friends.

66
00:02:23,313 --> 00:02:25,150
'Cause Valentine's
isn't just about boyfriends.

67
00:02:25,253 --> 00:02:27,825
If you don't have a boyfriend,
it's perfectly okay.

68
00:02:27,952 --> 00:02:29,610
I am so glad
we have boyfriends.

69
00:02:29,739 --> 00:02:32,698
Me, too. So where's Matt
taking you for Valentine's Day?

70
00:02:32,827 --> 00:02:35,232
Well, he hasn't officially
said anything yet,

71
00:02:35,317 --> 00:02:36,463
but I'm sure he will.

72
00:02:36,562 --> 00:02:39,848
We already declared
our love for each other, so...

73
00:02:40,231 --> 00:02:43,010
(Laughs)
<i>Yeah,</i> it's probably on.

74
00:02:43,098 --> 00:02:44,048
So on.

75
00:02:44,607 --> 00:02:48,133
Wow. Did you ever think we'd be
in high school with boyfriends?

76
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:50,637
I mean, me,
a big-time wrestlerette

77
00:02:50,709 --> 00:02:52,155
with a hotshot
wrestler boyfriend,

78
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:54,635
and you,
in freshman girls' chorus

79
00:02:54,726 --> 00:02:57,065
with your hot dog on a stick
boyfriend.

80
00:02:57,185 --> 00:02:59,892
We are ruling
this school! Yeah.

81
00:03:00,405 --> 00:03:01,512
Ooh, carnation...

82
00:03:08,670 --> 00:03:10,143
- Frankie, hi.
- Hey there.

83
00:03:10,245 --> 00:03:12,085
- Hey. - Well, isn't this a hoot,
running into you?

84
00:03:12,168 --> 00:03:14,312
What are the odds?
We should buy a lottery ticket.

85
00:03:14,405 --> 00:03:15,665
(All laugh)

86
00:03:15,808 --> 00:03:17,300
Hey, that's a lot of candy.

87
00:03:17,388 --> 00:03:18,422
Ugh. Brick's class.

88
00:03:18,505 --> 00:03:20,943
Apparently, it's not enough
to just give out cards anymore.

89
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:23,619
Now you gotta tape on little
candy hearts and lollipops.

90
00:03:23,727 --> 00:03:26,492
I could smack the mom
that started that tradition.

91
00:03:26,911 --> 00:03:28,752
Uh-oh. It might have been me.

92
00:03:28,883 --> 00:03:30,185
(All laugh)

93
00:03:30,506 --> 00:03:33,130
So you and Mike doing anything
special for Valentine's Day?

94
00:03:33,259 --> 00:03:36,252
Nah, we talked about it,
but let's face it-- It's not like

95
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,309
going out with our husbands
is that much fun anyway.

96
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,175
It's just staring at 'em
in a different location.

97
00:03:40,301 --> 00:03:41,369
(Both laugh)

98
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:43,085
You know, Valentine's
would be a lot more fun

99
00:03:43,165 --> 00:03:44,474
if you could go out
with your friends.

100
00:03:44,671 --> 00:03:46,608
Well, who says we can't?

101
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:49,364
I just got a coupon in the mail
for the Fountain Room.

102
00:03:49,521 --> 00:03:51,336
That place with the room
with the fountain?

103
00:03:51,436 --> 00:03:54,302
Mm-hmm. They're having this
amazing Valentine's Special.

104
00:03:54,408 --> 00:03:56,821
You get an appetizer,
choice of meat, soup, salad,

105
00:03:56,895 --> 00:03:59,857
endless bread bowl, pie,
and coffee, for $9.99.

106
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:02,024
You know what? Let's do it.

107
00:04:02,115 --> 00:04:03,701
Let's all go
to the fountain room together.

108
00:04:03,815 --> 00:04:04,825
Without the guys?

109
00:04:04,947 --> 00:04:06,854
No, we should probably
bring 'em,

110
00:04:06,937 --> 00:04:08,505
but this way, we'll have
each other to talk to.

111
00:04:08,621 --> 00:04:09,738
(Women laugh)

112
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,570
Relax. We're gonna buy it.

113
00:04:14,038 --> 00:04:15,163
He must be new.

114
00:04:17,973 --> 00:04:19,914
Dudes, it's, like,
a totally lame assignment.

115
00:04:20,019 --> 00:04:20,936
I mean, we're only juniors.

116
00:04:21,004 --> 00:04:22,994
What big, life-changing event
could we have even had?

117
00:04:23,188 --> 00:04:24,534
I know. It sucks.

118
00:04:24,679 --> 00:04:26,117
I'm probably just gonna write
about the time I got trapped

119
00:04:26,208 --> 00:04:28,084
under the ice at Patoka Lake.

120
00:04:28,237 --> 00:04:29,524
That counts, right?

121
00:04:29,967 --> 00:04:30,843
What?

122
00:04:30,935 --> 00:04:31,492
Yeah.

123
00:04:31,572 --> 00:04:32,500
I can't decide between the time

124
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,830
I helped deliver my baby sister
at the carpet store,

125
00:04:34,951 --> 00:04:35,960
or the time
I was pronounced dead

126
00:04:36,055 --> 00:04:38,031
for 2 minutes when I was 6.

127
00:04:39,015 --> 00:04:40,514
What do you guys like better?

128
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,688
<i>Sue was sure</i>
<i>Matt was going to ask her out</i>

129
00:04:46,769 --> 00:04:49,049
<i>for Valentine's Day,</i>
<i>so she played it cool.</i>

130
00:04:49,352 --> 00:04:51,171
<i>Well, Sue cool.</i>
(Shifts gears)

131
00:04:51,987 --> 00:04:55,257
Sue, we've been in love
for almost three weeks now,

132
00:04:55,514 --> 00:04:56,399
and I was wondering

133
00:04:56,498 --> 00:04:58,224
if you were doing anything
for Valentine's Day.

134
00:04:58,973 --> 00:05:00,068
I am not.

135
00:05:00,336 --> 00:05:02,834
I am not at all.

136
00:05:02,963 --> 00:05:04,097
Excellent.

137
00:05:04,491 --> 00:05:06,835
I'd like to take you to this
great Italian place that I know.

138
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:08,471
I have a meet the next day,
so I can't eat,

139
00:05:08,577 --> 00:05:11,336
but I'd really enjoy
watching my lady eat.

140
00:05:12,772 --> 00:05:14,675
(Gasps) That sounds great.

141
00:05:21,298 --> 00:05:22,299
(Door squeaks)

142
00:05:26,418 --> 00:05:28,694
- Sue, are you okay?
- No, not at all.

143
00:05:28,812 --> 00:05:31,806
All of a sudden, Matt's turned
into the world's worst kisser.

144
00:05:32,358 --> 00:05:33,218
What do you mean?

145
00:05:33,322 --> 00:05:36,604
Out of nowhere,
he puts his--his tongue...

146
00:05:36,776 --> 00:05:38,650
Into... my mouth.

147
00:05:38,769 --> 00:05:41,833
Oh, my God. What is that?
Who does that?

148
00:05:42,065 --> 00:05:44,054
- Well-- - I can't help
but feel bad for him.

149
00:05:44,139 --> 00:05:46,257
It's like he totally
forgot how to kiss.

150
00:05:46,365 --> 00:05:50,735
I mean, what place does <i>a tongue</i>
have in <i>kissing?</i>

151
00:05:50,863 --> 00:05:52,443
What should I do?

152
00:05:52,616 --> 00:05:54,363
I mean, I don't want
to embarrass him,

153
00:05:54,464 --> 00:05:56,435
but he has to be told.
(Gasps)

154
00:05:56,561 --> 00:05:59,671
Wait. I think I saw something
on kickinitteenstyle.com

155
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:01,291
on how to tell your boyfriend
he's a bad kisser.

156
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:03,296
I'm gonna go check it out.

157
00:06:05,348 --> 00:06:07,147
<i>I really need</i>
<i>to talk to Sue more.</i>

158
00:06:08,005 --> 00:06:08,709
(Sighs)

159
00:06:16,355 --> 00:06:18,807
Sue, I'd prefer not
to yell like mom does,

160
00:06:18,963 --> 00:06:20,202
but you're hogging
the computer,

161
00:06:20,286 --> 00:06:22,010
and I need to research
my paper on love,

162
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:23,805
so if I have to,
I will go there.

163
00:06:23,986 --> 00:06:26,039
Let me ask you,
if you were a bad kisser,

164
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:28,226
which one would you rather hear
from your girlfriend--

165
00:06:29,051 --> 00:06:30,960
"A"-- "Ew! No!"

166
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:32,807
"B"--"Would you like to peruse

167
00:06:32,908 --> 00:06:35,030
this pamphlet
I found on kissing?"

168
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:37,608
Or "C"--"how about
we take a break from kissing

169
00:06:37,697 --> 00:06:39,282
and go get a fro-yo?"

170
00:06:39,901 --> 00:06:41,310
As much as I love
a good pamphlet,

171
00:06:41,415 --> 00:06:42,641
I'd go with fro-yo.

172
00:06:42,794 --> 00:06:44,420
(Whispers) Fro-yo.

173
00:06:47,283 --> 00:06:48,724
(Taps key)

174
00:06:49,872 --> 00:06:50,649
Hey.

175
00:06:50,742 --> 00:06:53,280
Oh, hey. New plan. We're going
out for Valentine's Day.

176
00:06:53,536 --> 00:06:55,250
What? Oh, no.

177
00:06:55,395 --> 00:06:58,392
I really liked our old plan--
The TV and the chicken.

178
00:06:58,525 --> 00:07:00,588
No, no. This is good.
It's not just us.

179
00:07:00,684 --> 00:07:01,912
Ron and Bill
are gonna be there.

180
00:07:02,003 --> 00:07:03,478
Oh, okay. That's fine, then.

181
00:07:04,046 --> 00:07:07,570
All right. I need everyone
in here, like, now.

182
00:07:14,766 --> 00:07:15,735
What's going on?

183
00:07:15,854 --> 00:07:20,333
Okay. I finished my speech
on a life-changing event.

184
00:07:20,423 --> 00:07:21,671
I think I really nailed it,

185
00:07:21,790 --> 00:07:23,926
and I kind of want
to practice on you guys.

186
00:07:24,208 --> 00:07:25,193
Do I have to?

187
00:07:25,386 --> 00:07:27,634
He didn't help me
take the tree out.

188
00:07:27,727 --> 00:07:28,605
Ahem.

189
00:07:29,625 --> 00:07:31,736
"My life-changing event,
by Axl Heck."

190
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:36,017
"There was a moment
not that long ago,"

191
00:07:36,116 --> 00:07:37,646
when an event happened
that changed my life,

192
00:07:37,789 --> 00:07:39,046
a moment that made me question

193
00:07:39,156 --> 00:07:41,006
everything I knew
about myself to be true.

194
00:07:41,128 --> 00:07:43,013
I thought
this girl was really hot,

195
00:07:43,127 --> 00:07:44,884
and I asked her out,
and she said, 'no, '

196
00:07:44,987 --> 00:07:47,137
and then I was like,
'why? Am I not hot?'

197
00:07:47,265 --> 00:07:48,191
and I couldn't believe it,

198
00:07:48,312 --> 00:07:49,410
'cause a lot of people
think I'm hot,

199
00:07:49,553 --> 00:07:50,860
but maybe I wasn't hot.

200
00:07:50,999 --> 00:07:53,315
Maybe I was wrong
about being hot.

201
00:07:53,464 --> 00:07:54,938
So I stood
in front of the mirror,

202
00:07:55,035 --> 00:07:57,111
staring at myself
for, like, eight hours,

203
00:07:57,208 --> 00:08:00,158
asking myself,
'am I hot or not hot?'

204
00:08:00,304 --> 00:08:01,874
and as I reflected
on my reflection,

205
00:08:01,961 --> 00:08:04,790
I realized, 'you're the ax-man.
Of course you're hot.'

206
00:08:05,202 --> 00:08:06,406
so then, like,
I asked her out again,

207
00:08:06,517 --> 00:08:08,431
"and she said, 'yes.'
The end."

208
00:08:10,299 --> 00:08:11,685
Enjoy summer school.

209
00:08:12,169 --> 00:08:13,638
Ohh, this is all your fault!

210
00:08:14,512 --> 00:08:16,979
You know why I haven't had
a life-changing event?

211
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,673
'Cause nothing in my life
has happened-- Nothing!

212
00:08:19,843 --> 00:08:21,783
I mean, we're not
rich enough to travel,

213
00:08:21,863 --> 00:08:23,124
we're not poor enough
to live out of our car,

214
00:08:23,237 --> 00:08:24,908
mom's not on the Internet,
stripping for money,

215
00:08:24,996 --> 00:08:26,999
and dad doesn't get drunk
and beat anyone.

216
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:28,141
Not yet.

217
00:08:28,926 --> 00:08:31,763
(Sighs) Axl, I'm sure you have
plenty of things to write about

218
00:08:31,875 --> 00:08:33,881
if you just think
about it. (Sighs)

219
00:08:34,588 --> 00:08:37,194
What about the time you helped
out at the homeless shelter?

220
00:08:37,675 --> 00:08:38,515
Shrug.

221
00:08:38,632 --> 00:08:40,446
How about everything you did
to help out Aunt Edie?

222
00:08:40,546 --> 00:08:41,392
Yawn.

223
00:08:41,738 --> 00:08:44,418
Well, I have tons of things
that changed my life--

224
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,254
Wrestlerettes,
Justin Bieber's Christmas album,

225
00:08:47,363 --> 00:08:48,426
dating Matt...

226
00:08:48,521 --> 00:08:51,543
That e-mail grandma forwarded me
about that wild pony...

227
00:08:51,674 --> 00:08:52,651
What about books?

228
00:08:52,735 --> 00:08:54,892
Is there any book that's had
an impact on your life?

229
00:08:55,026 --> 00:08:56,076
Oh, what am I saying?

230
00:08:56,186 --> 00:08:58,803
Hey, what about the summer you
spent at the lake with grandpa,

231
00:08:58,937 --> 00:09:00,421
and you helped him
fix his boat?

232
00:09:00,835 --> 00:09:01,810
Oh, yeah.

233
00:09:02,350 --> 00:09:03,526
I remember that.

234
00:09:04,416 --> 00:09:06,616
Oh, I got so tan that summer,
I was really hot.

235
00:09:07,227 --> 00:09:08,816
(Sighs) You got nothin'.

236
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:11,712
I know! And Darrin died
for 2 minutes when he was 6.

237
00:09:11,886 --> 00:09:13,672
What? He did?

238
00:09:13,774 --> 00:09:15,290
His mother never told me this.

239
00:09:15,386 --> 00:09:16,685
(Brick) - What happened?
(Mike) - When was this?

240
00:09:17,146 --> 00:09:18,220
You guys suck.

241
00:09:28,436 --> 00:09:30,844
(Axl) This is my brother,
and he's been very sick

242
00:09:30,935 --> 00:09:33,034
for a long time,
with a horrible disease.

243
00:09:33,154 --> 00:09:34,812
Despite all the "walks for hope"
and "fun runs,"

244
00:09:34,899 --> 00:09:36,827
there is, as yet, no cure.

245
00:09:36,976 --> 00:09:37,732
(Coughs)

246
00:09:38,733 --> 00:09:40,458
This has been such
a life-changing event for me,

247
00:09:40,604 --> 00:09:42,175
his brother, Axl Heck,

248
00:09:42,311 --> 00:09:43,779
Mrs. Johnson's
sixth-period English.

249
00:09:44,941 --> 00:09:48,311
It's the not knowing
that's the hard part.

250
00:09:48,607 --> 00:09:50,003
Oh, and the dying.

251
00:09:50,628 --> 00:09:52,225
Actually, they're both hard.

252
00:09:52,748 --> 00:09:55,410
I have to give my brother
all these medicines every day.

253
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:58,840
If I could give any advice,

254
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:03,791
it'd be live, love, laugh.

255
00:10:04,332 --> 00:10:05,477
Some would call it burden

256
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:08,175
to care for a brother so sick
with this horrible disease.

257
00:10:08,411 --> 00:10:10,303
I call it life-changing.

258
00:10:12,210 --> 00:10:15,104
I just hope I can one day
frolic in the sea.

259
00:10:15,610 --> 00:10:16,568
That's all.

260
00:10:16,954 --> 00:10:18,156
One day.

261
00:10:19,095 --> 00:10:20,113
In the sea.

262
00:10:20,669 --> 00:10:23,396
(Whispers)
So friggin' life-changing.

263
00:10:24,184 --> 00:10:26,784
<i>(Mandolin playing)</i> (Laughter)

264
00:10:26,867 --> 00:10:27,742
(Mike) Oh, and last winter,

265
00:10:27,843 --> 00:10:30,764
he tries to hang glide
off our roof with a trash bag.

266
00:10:31,972 --> 00:10:34,797
Lucky he landed on Darrin,
who tried it before him,

267
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:36,622
with kites taped to his arms.

268
00:10:37,093 --> 00:10:37,897
(Laughter)

269
00:10:38,264 --> 00:10:40,268
The thing about teenage boys--
They're just so stupid.

270
00:10:40,375 --> 00:10:41,144
I heard someone say

271
00:10:41,262 --> 00:10:43,549
that if you have
a girl first and then a boy,

272
00:10:43,708 --> 00:10:45,966
you'll swear
the boy is brain-damaged.

273
00:10:46,269 --> 00:10:46,931
(Laughter) No, no.

274
00:10:47,048 --> 00:10:49,049
Teenage girls are way worse,
'cause they're impressed

275
00:10:49,161 --> 00:10:51,405
by the stupid things
teenage boys do.

276
00:10:51,603 --> 00:10:52,760
Thank God.

277
00:10:52,892 --> 00:10:53,933
(Laughter)

278
00:10:54,058 --> 00:10:56,718
Excuse me. Would you like to buy
a rose for your sweetheart?

279
00:10:56,863 --> 00:10:58,014
Uh-oh. Is she here?

280
00:10:58,177 --> 00:10:59,561
(Laughter)

281
00:10:59,674 --> 00:11:00,871
Very funny.

282
00:11:01,262 --> 00:11:02,469
Sure.

283
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:03,411
This is fun, isn't it?

284
00:11:03,509 --> 00:11:04,554
Yeah, good meat.

285
00:11:06,748 --> 00:11:07,738
Aw.

286
00:11:08,256 --> 00:11:10,040
I mean, you know,
I did some bonehead things

287
00:11:10,145 --> 00:11:12,205
when I was young.
I mean, we all did, right?

288
00:11:12,330 --> 00:11:13,860
Oh. I'll take one.

289
00:11:15,497 --> 00:11:16,516
(Frankie and Nancy) Aw.

290
00:11:17,223 --> 00:11:20,070
I know we all did stuff,
but last week, I walk in,

291
00:11:20,190 --> 00:11:23,869
he's in his bed, trying to
cook bacon with the iron...

292
00:11:23,967 --> 00:11:25,076
(Laughter)

293
00:11:25,373 --> 00:11:26,280
No, we're good.

294
00:11:26,753 --> 00:11:28,827
And then he says, uh,
I should be thanking him

295
00:11:28,975 --> 00:11:30,438
because he's not
dirtying a pan.

296
00:11:30,577 --> 00:11:32,479
(Laughter)

297
00:11:32,684 --> 00:11:34,102
So how was the bacon?

298
00:11:34,228 --> 00:11:35,918
You know what? Not bad.

299
00:11:36,176 --> 00:11:37,167
(Laughter)

300
00:11:42,489 --> 00:11:44,492
(Door squeaks)

301
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,318
I know I said I wanted
to stay home tonight,

302
00:11:46,409 --> 00:11:48,655
but I'm glad we went.
I had a good time.

303
00:11:48,746 --> 00:11:51,696
Great. I'm glad.
I'm glad you had a good time.

304
00:11:51,786 --> 00:11:52,818
I really did.

305
00:11:53,108 --> 00:11:55,332
Hey, maybe we should try our
anniversary with other couples.

306
00:11:55,452 --> 00:11:56,688
Yeah, maybe.

307
00:11:56,831 --> 00:11:58,035
(Sighs) You coming to bed?

308
00:11:58,191 --> 00:11:59,704
No. I don't think so.

309
00:11:59,895 --> 00:12:01,720
I'm going to do
some other things right now

310
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:02,759
besides going to bed.

311
00:12:02,923 --> 00:12:04,358
Okay.
Don't stay up too late.

312
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,103
Oh, and hey,
happy Valentine's Day.

313
00:12:09,352 --> 00:12:10,725
(Sighs)

314
00:12:12,485 --> 00:12:15,570
Okay, well,
thanks for a great V-Day.

315
00:12:15,753 --> 00:12:16,832
I gotta go.

316
00:12:17,006 --> 00:12:18,013
Sue, wait.

317
00:12:24,467 --> 00:12:25,939
You know what?

318
00:12:26,030 --> 00:12:28,136
These leftovers
will not be good tomorrow,

319
00:12:28,264 --> 00:12:30,089
and they are
too delicious to waste.

320
00:12:31,082 --> 00:12:32,118
Ohh.

321
00:12:32,434 --> 00:12:33,270
Mmm.

322
00:12:33,459 --> 00:12:35,609
Garlic is the best.
(Laughs)

323
00:12:36,132 --> 00:12:37,988
Mm. Of course
my breath probably reeks.

324
00:12:38,310 --> 00:12:41,000
I'm a wrestler.
I'll fight through it.

325
00:12:44,423 --> 00:12:45,744
You gonna finish that?

326
00:12:50,817 --> 00:12:51,251
(Door closes)

327
00:12:51,349 --> 00:12:52,798
Oh, my God.
He did it again.

328
00:12:52,923 --> 00:12:54,783
Hey. Nice flowers.

329
00:12:54,916 --> 00:12:57,394
Lucky for you, I didn't get any,
so the vase is free.

330
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,277
This time, I tried
to keep my mouth closed,

331
00:12:59,384 --> 00:13:01,187
but it still got
in there somehow.

332
00:13:01,301 --> 00:13:03,374
It's almost like
he's doing it on purpose.

333
00:13:03,569 --> 00:13:04,533
(Sighs)

334
00:13:05,215 --> 00:13:06,894
Yeah. Sue...
(Clatter)

335
00:13:07,068 --> 00:13:10,250
Here's the thing.
He <i>is</i> doing it on purpose.

336
00:13:10,450 --> 00:13:11,885
What? Why?

337
00:13:12,066 --> 00:13:14,627
Why would he do something
like that? It's so mean.

338
00:13:14,787 --> 00:13:17,799
Yeah, well, it might
seem mean to you now,

339
00:13:17,876 --> 00:13:20,349
but, you know,
some people sort of like it.

340
00:13:20,650 --> 00:13:22,381
Who? Who would like that?

341
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:25,286
It's like having an eel
<i>in your mouth.</i>

342
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:26,989
Oh, come on, Sue.
There are two girls

343
00:13:27,088 --> 00:13:28,838
that are pregnant
in your class right now.

344
00:13:28,935 --> 00:13:30,563
You never heard
of french kissing?

345
00:13:31,323 --> 00:13:34,094
Whoa, wait a minute.
That's french kissing?

346
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:35,695
Yeah. What did you
think it was?

347
00:13:36,436 --> 00:13:39,331
I thought it was kissing
during a rainbow.

348
00:13:39,614 --> 00:13:42,403
Oh, wow. We really
should talk more often.

349
00:13:43,474 --> 00:13:45,712
So... do you and dad
french kiss?

350
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:46,801
What?

351
00:13:47,097 --> 00:13:50,088
Oh, well... (Mouth full)
Not for a while now,

352
00:13:50,281 --> 00:13:52,144
and certainly not tonight.

353
00:14:04,316 --> 00:14:05,878
You want to know why I'm mad?

354
00:14:06,291 --> 00:14:06,953
What?

355
00:14:07,072 --> 00:14:08,052
The rose, Mike.

356
00:14:08,208 --> 00:14:09,505
What-- what time is this?

357
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:11,703
I'm the only one last night
that didn't get a rose.

358
00:14:11,810 --> 00:14:13,057
Hold on. Is this for real?

359
00:14:13,225 --> 00:14:15,892
Are you really upset,
or is this, like, a joke?

360
00:14:15,991 --> 00:14:18,498
Oh, yeah, it's a joke,
a very famous joke.

361
00:14:18,594 --> 00:14:20,221
Ha ha ha ha! Hilarious.
(Curtain rings swoosh)

362
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:23,166
Come on, Frankie.
We don't buy into that crap.

363
00:14:23,301 --> 00:14:25,206
We always laugh
about how those rose ladies try

364
00:14:25,298 --> 00:14:27,363
to guilt you into buying a rose.
It's stupid.

365
00:14:27,464 --> 00:14:28,656
Well, of course it's stupid.

366
00:14:28,749 --> 00:14:29,655
Then why'd you wake me up?

367
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:32,262
Because Ron bought Nancy one,
Bill bought Paula one,

368
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:34,548
and while they're sitting there
twirling their pretty roses,

369
00:14:34,641 --> 00:14:37,511
I'm stuck waving around
a breadstick like an idiot.

370
00:14:37,605 --> 00:14:39,132
It was embarrassing.

371
00:14:39,231 --> 00:14:40,344
So they're big suckers

372
00:14:40,447 --> 00:14:42,251
who cave at the slightest
bit of pressure.

373
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:44,404
I'm proud of myself.
I stuck to my guns.

374
00:14:44,505 --> 00:14:46,052
Oh, yeah,
you're a real inspiration.

375
00:14:46,157 --> 00:14:47,775
My knight in shining...
(Blows raspberry)

376
00:14:47,892 --> 00:14:50,879
You think flowers are
a waste of money, too.

377
00:14:50,974 --> 00:14:52,872
You said so yourself.
The whole thing's a scam.

378
00:14:52,976 --> 00:14:54,041
I know it's a scam.

379
00:14:54,138 --> 00:14:55,274
Well, then why
are you so upset?!

380
00:14:55,375 --> 00:14:57,947
Because all my friends
got a flower, and I didn't!

381
00:14:58,045 --> 00:15:00,890
What, are you in high school?
Are you afraid I don't like you?

382
00:15:01,034 --> 00:15:04,406
News flash, Frankie-- I like you.
I <i>like you</i> like you.

383
00:15:04,727 --> 00:15:05,485
(Door closes)

384
00:15:06,501 --> 00:15:08,102
My prognosis is grim,

385
00:15:08,219 --> 00:15:10,657
but there is
a small ray of hope.

386
00:15:10,822 --> 00:15:14,414
I'm on the waiting list
for the Mayo Clinic. (Coughs)

387
00:15:14,704 --> 00:15:17,138
If things don't work out
at the Mayonnaise Clinic,

388
00:15:17,270 --> 00:15:18,513
I don't know
what we're gonna do.

389
00:15:18,634 --> 00:15:19,596
(Frankie) What are you doing?

390
00:15:19,704 --> 00:15:21,325
Mom, shh!
We're filming here.

391
00:15:21,408 --> 00:15:23,385
I'm working on my "life-changing
event" project for school.

392
00:15:23,502 --> 00:15:24,557
Seriously, Axl?

393
00:15:24,661 --> 00:15:26,376
You are not doing this
for your school project.

394
00:15:26,519 --> 00:15:27,699
Your brother's not dying.

395
00:15:27,847 --> 00:15:30,141
My mom's in deep denial.

396
00:15:30,324 --> 00:15:32,105
(Mike) You know what, Frankie?
You want flowers?

397
00:15:32,257 --> 00:15:33,495
Fine, I'll get you flowers.

398
00:15:33,596 --> 00:15:35,190
I don't want
your guilt flowers!

399
00:15:35,293 --> 00:15:37,538
They're not guilt flowers,
'cause I don't feel guilty.

400
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:39,637
I feel good!
I stuck to my guns!

401
00:15:39,764 --> 00:15:42,280
- He hides his pain with false bravado.
- Oh, yeah. Here we go. Big hero.

402
00:15:42,379 --> 00:15:44,284
It was Valentine's Day, Mike.
Valentine's Day.

403
00:15:44,385 --> 00:15:46,364
It would have been a romantic
gesture. That's all I'm saying.

404
00:15:46,506 --> 00:15:47,626
Romance?

405
00:15:47,842 --> 00:15:50,112
You're the one who had no
interest in spending Valentine's

406
00:15:50,225 --> 00:15:52,921
with me until you invited
your lady friends along.

407
00:15:53,021 --> 00:15:54,693
Maybe you should have
asked Nancy and Paula

408
00:15:54,796 --> 00:15:55,824
to buy you a flower.

409
00:15:55,915 --> 00:15:57,114
That is not true!

410
00:15:57,221 --> 00:15:59,354
- That is so not true.
- It's like this every day--

411
00:15:59,447 --> 00:16:01,936
- I cannot believe you said that. - The
arguing, the tension, so life-changing.

412
00:16:02,042 --> 00:16:04,022
I wanted to do something with
you, but you acted all tired

413
00:16:04,125 --> 00:16:05,382
and talked me
into separate bedrooms

414
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,686
with buckets of chicken.

415
00:16:06,815 --> 00:16:09,364
You-- Hey, you were
on board with the buckets

416
00:16:09,481 --> 00:16:10,858
just as much as I was!

417
00:16:10,981 --> 00:16:12,812
You're not romantic, Mike, okay?
You're not.

418
00:16:12,899 --> 00:16:14,724
(Groans) You never have been.
Fine. Whatever.

419
00:16:14,836 --> 00:16:17,321
See? Right there. That is
why I hate Valentine's Day!

420
00:16:17,433 --> 00:16:19,726
Yeah, Valentine's Day
hates you right back!

421
00:16:19,842 --> 00:16:22,148
Oh, no. I think they might
be getting a divorce.

422
00:16:22,255 --> 00:16:24,508
Nothing changes a young,
innocent life more than that.

423
00:16:24,656 --> 00:16:26,792
- Axl, would you stop filming us?!
- Turn that camera off.

424
00:16:26,889 --> 00:16:28,993
(Brick) Axl, do you want me
to die or not?

425
00:16:29,096 --> 00:16:30,749
'Cause I'm gonna be late for school.
(Doors close)

426
00:16:31,001 --> 00:16:33,809
So, uh, thanks for the ride.
I'll see you tomorrow!

427
00:16:33,926 --> 00:16:34,838
(Blows kiss)

428
00:16:34,944 --> 00:16:36,712
Sue, w-what's going on?

429
00:16:37,427 --> 00:16:39,162
It's like you've been trying
to avoid me or something.

430
00:16:39,464 --> 00:16:42,312
Okay, Matt.
Here's the thing.

431
00:16:43,058 --> 00:16:44,257
There's something
I have to tell you,

432
00:16:44,352 --> 00:16:47,335
and I really hope it doesn't
change things between us.

433
00:16:48,172 --> 00:16:51,984
I'm an American girl,
so I just want to kiss American.

434
00:16:52,485 --> 00:16:55,046
If you want
to kiss... international,

435
00:16:55,182 --> 00:16:57,846
then you'll have to
find someone else.

436
00:16:59,050 --> 00:17:00,152
Oh, thank God.

437
00:17:00,701 --> 00:17:01,714
You're not mad?

438
00:17:02,103 --> 00:17:05,216
No. Your braces were
ripping my tongue to shreds.

439
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,357
It's kept me from eating,
so I made weight this week,

440
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:09,055
but I didn't tell you,

441
00:17:09,137 --> 00:17:10,875
'cause I didn't want
to hurt your feelings.

442
00:17:12,497 --> 00:17:16,104
Really? That's so sweet!

443
00:17:16,228 --> 00:17:18,090
But kickinitteenstyle.com
says that

444
00:17:18,188 --> 00:17:22,329
a relationship will only succeed
if it's built on total honesty.

445
00:17:22,509 --> 00:17:23,523
Okay.

446
00:17:24,184 --> 00:17:25,951
Sometimes
your hair smells funny.

447
00:17:26,083 --> 00:17:29,147
Oh! My mom accidentally
bought dog shampoo.

448
00:17:29,265 --> 00:17:30,839
She says we have to use it up
till it's gone.

449
00:17:32,091 --> 00:17:34,047
(Both laugh)

450
00:17:43,117 --> 00:17:44,071
(Brick)
Oh, good. You're here.

451
00:17:44,175 --> 00:17:47,568
(Door closes) You can sit over
there next to mom. Dad! Axl!

452
00:17:48,182 --> 00:17:49,107
Why am I doing this?

453
00:17:49,248 --> 00:17:51,241
We have to listen
to your brother's paper.

454
00:17:51,365 --> 00:17:53,042
You listened to Axl's.

455
00:17:53,133 --> 00:17:54,939
In the interest
of not showing favoritism,

456
00:17:55,048 --> 00:17:57,243
you could be
a little more enthusiastic.

457
00:17:57,372 --> 00:17:59,919
Is this a new thing?
We have to listen to papers now?

458
00:18:00,111 --> 00:18:01,480
(Clears throat)

459
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:05,026
"What is love?
Shakespeare tells us that"

460
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:08,164
'love looks not with the eyes,
but with the mind.'

461
00:18:08,302 --> 00:18:11,758
I'm only 10 and have yet
to experience great love,

462
00:18:11,870 --> 00:18:14,877
so I chose to write about
the only love I'm familiar with,

463
00:18:15,058 --> 00:18:17,309
the love my parents share.

464
00:18:17,757 --> 00:18:21,030
"It's not a new love
filled with burning passion."

465
00:18:21,154 --> 00:18:21,920
(Frankie and Mike scoff)

466
00:18:22,023 --> 00:18:24,291
"My sister says they don't even
French kiss anymore."

467
00:18:24,390 --> 00:18:25,173
- Sue.
- Brick!

468
00:18:25,282 --> 00:18:27,524
"But it's the little things
I see them do for each other"

469
00:18:27,637 --> 00:18:30,774
that tells me what love is,
like in the car,

470
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:33,339
when my mom puts her hand
on the back of my dad's neck

471
00:18:33,425 --> 00:18:34,483
and massages it...

472
00:18:34,656 --> 00:18:38,405
Or when my dad warms up
my mom's car and scrapes the ice

473
00:18:38,507 --> 00:18:40,776
off her windshield
on cold mornings...

474
00:18:41,202 --> 00:18:43,778
And how they've learned
to communicate with each other,

475
00:18:43,894 --> 00:18:45,663
"using their own
special language."

476
00:18:45,779 --> 00:18:46,886
(Mumbles)

477
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:48,412
(Mumbles, clears throat)

478
00:18:48,668 --> 00:18:50,238
"It's true we don't
have a lot of money,"

479
00:18:50,384 --> 00:18:52,288
but I like to think,
even if we did,

480
00:18:52,419 --> 00:18:55,635
my parents would still be
at home, hanging out together--

481
00:18:55,898 --> 00:18:59,470
Of course in a much nicer house with a
jacuzzi soaking tub." (Mouths words)

482
00:18:59,686 --> 00:19:00,602
(Mouths words)
"If you ask people

483
00:19:00,696 --> 00:19:02,135
what they think
are the greatest loves stories,

484
00:19:02,244 --> 00:19:05,604
they'll say Romeo and Juliet,
or Hermione and Ron Weasley,

485
00:19:05,718 --> 00:19:07,099
and those are fine,

486
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:10,837
but if you ask me,
great love stories can be small,

487
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:12,942
"like my mom and dad's."

488
00:19:14,128 --> 00:19:15,978
Oh, Brick.

489
00:19:16,519 --> 00:19:19,274
That was really amazing.

490
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:20,818
Really good job, buddy.

491
00:19:22,543 --> 00:19:23,747
<i>What?</i>

492
00:19:23,883 --> 00:19:25,453
You guys liked
that snooze fest,

493
00:19:25,555 --> 00:19:27,671
but you didn't like my paper
about not being hot enough?

494
00:19:27,801 --> 00:19:29,433
Oh. I see
what's going on here.

495
00:19:29,526 --> 00:19:32,667
His paper's all about you,
so it's good. Whatever.

496
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:37,253
<i>It turned out Brick's paper</i>
<i>affected all of us.</i>

497
00:19:37,625 --> 00:19:38,575
(Sighs)

498
00:19:39,135 --> 00:19:40,048
Ohh.

499
00:19:40,212 --> 00:19:41,163
(Laughs)

500
00:19:41,410 --> 00:19:44,857
<i>Even Axl found an appreciation</i>
<i>for his brother's work.</i>

501
00:19:44,964 --> 00:19:48,460
"Sure, it's easy to get trapped
under ice. That's obvious."

502
00:19:48,843 --> 00:19:51,718
But when I think about
what's really life-changing,

503
00:19:51,845 --> 00:19:54,173
I think about
the little things,

504
00:19:54,388 --> 00:19:58,112
like when my mom rubs
my dad's neck when he's driving,

505
00:19:58,223 --> 00:20:00,548
or the way my dad scrapes ice
off my mom's windshield

506
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:01,874
on frosty mornings

507
00:20:02,051 --> 00:20:04,561
or their own secret language.

508
00:20:07,721 --> 00:20:09,628
"Yeah, we don't have a lot
of money, but even if we did..."

509
00:20:09,717 --> 00:20:12,577
<i>Point is, we'd all survived</i>
<i>another Valentine's Day.</i>

510
00:20:12,701 --> 00:20:15,135
<i>'Cause let's face it--</i>
<i>It's a high-pressure holiday.</i>

511
00:20:15,325 --> 00:20:16,286
<i>Lucky when you plan</i>

512
00:20:16,375 --> 00:20:18,120
<i>on loving someone</i>
<i>for the rest of your life,</i>

513
00:20:18,229 --> 00:20:20,392
<i>you got a lot of other days</i>
<i>to get it right.</i>

514
00:20:22,815 --> 00:20:31,170
